Reason: Both queries weight contribution amounts by the HUD cross‑walk’s total_ratio and restrict donors to NY and tracts to Kings County, but 1result.sql fails to exclude NaN contribution amounts—these propagate through SUM/AVG and can corrupt or nullify tract‑level averages. 2result.sql explicitly filters out NaN values with `NOT IS_NAN(transaction_amt)`, so its aggregates are mathematically valid; therefore it is the correct choice.